# OpenVPN Dashboard — Caddy reverse proxy configuration
#
# Caddy automatically obtains and renews TLS certificates from Let's Encrypt
# (or ZeroSSL) with zero configuration required. Simply replace "your-domain.com"
# with your actual domain and point DNS at this server — HTTPS is handled for you.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Install Caddy: https://caddyserver.com/docs/install
#   2. Replace "your-domain.com" with your actual domain.
#   3. Copy or reference this file in your Caddyfile (or use it as the entire Caddyfile):
#        sudo cp Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   4. Reload Caddy:
#        sudo systemctl reload caddy
#   Caddy will automatically obtain a TLS certificate on first request.

your-domain.com {
    reverse_proxy localhost:3000
}
